{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And He afflicted you and let you hunger, etc.</b> One needs to know what connection the words <b>and He afflicted you</b>, etc., have with <b>and He fed you</b>, etc., for according to the plain sense of the words it would denote a disparagement of the manna, indicating that eating the manna was on account of hunger — but this is not so, for we find that the Torah abundantly praised the manna, as stated (Numbers 11:7) ״וְהַמָּן״ etc., and our Sages of blessed memory said (Sifrei ad loc.) that everything written about it speaks in its praise. It is also the sustenance of the angels (Yoma 75b), as it says ״לֶחֶם אַבִּירִים אָכַל אִישׁ״. And it appears that here too the verse proclaims the praise of the manna, for foods are of two types: there is a food suitable for everyone, whether healthy or sick, because it is clean of spoilage and is entirely absorbed into the limbs and is easy to digest and nourishes a person; and there is a food suitable only for the healthy, but for a sick person it would harm him and destroy him. Therefore the verse says concerning the manna <b>and He afflicted you and let you hunger and fed you</b>, etc. — meaning: <b>and He afflicted you</b> refers to the affliction of the journey; <b>and let you hunger</b> refers to the affliction of lack of food. Now it is well known that one who fasts on the road — his powers are weakened, the power of digestion and the power of assimilation; and when a person eats food that is somewhat difficult to digest, it will harm him greatly. Also, when a person is hungry and eats to the point of satiety, it will bring him to illness. And our eyes see that on a day when a person fasts, at the time of eating he cannot eat to the full desire of his appetite. And He said <b>and He fed you the manna</b> — behold, this is praise of the food, that it is something suitable even for the afflicted and the hungry, aside from the perceived quality that it was like a wafer in honey."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:03.196314821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}